      "question": "Do I pay federal tax on forgiven student loans?",
      "answer": "It depends on the type of discharge and the date it occurs. Student loan debt canceled after December 31, 2020, and before January 1, 2026, was excluded from gross income under a temporary federal rule. Discharges outside that window are generally taxable unless they meet an exclusion under Section 108, such as working in certain professions, death, disability, or taxpayer insolvency."
